{title: Love Lifted Me}
{artist: James Rowe / Howard E. Smith}
{genre: Gospel}
{flow: Response}
{style: Traditional}
{key: G}
{key_original: Bb}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
I was [G]sinking deep in sin, far from the [C]peaceful [G]shore
Very [G]deeply stained within, sinking to [D7]rise no [G]more
But the [G]Master of the sea heard my de[C]spairing [G]cry
From the [G]waters lifted me, now [D7]safe am [G]I
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Love lifted me! [C]Love lifted [G]me!
When nothing [G]else could help, [D7]Love lifted [G]me!
[G]Love lifted me! [C]Love lifted [G]me!
When nothing [G]else could help, [D7]Love lifted [G]me!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
All my [G]heart to Him I give, ever to Him I'll [C]cling [G]
In His [G]blessed presence live, ever His [D7]praises [G]sing
Love so [G]mighty and so true, merits my [C]soul's best [G]songs
Faithful, [G]loving service, too, to [D7]Him be[G]longs
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
Souls in [G]danger, look above, Jesus com[C]pletely [G]saves
He will [G]lift you by His love, out of the [D7]angry [G]waves
He's the [G]Master of the sea, billows His [C]will o[G]bey
He your [G]Saviour wants to be, be [D7]saved to[G]day
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
